  "body": "PR705 leaves nine fixed eight-call Clifford register words unclassified when equal group products have different accumulated Fourier ranks. This extends its determinant argument by choosing arbitrary Laurent path weights and requiring homogeneity only for coefficients forbidden by the endpoint. The resulting exact certificate excludes **`evolved-27` for every invertible choice of its four 3-by-3 scalar blocks**, even without a shared final frame per input column.\n\nThe certificate has interior weights `(1,0,1), (-1,-1,0), (0,0,0)`, row potentials `(-1,0,0)` and column potentials `(0,1,1)`. Its scalar weighted determinant has degree zero, while every permitted determinant term has valuation at least one. `PROOF.md` gives the general argument over a formal group algebra, including why cancellation of forbidden coefficients is preserved.\n\nAcross all nine unresolved words, one global and 918 frame-specific certificates exclude 1,093 of 1,152 endpoint frame triples; **59 remain unclassified**. Of the exclusions, 865 already follow from the elementary allowed-entry matching test. The weighted criterion adds **228 exclusions beyond that baseline**. No exhaustive comparison against predecessor support/polynomial methods is claimed.\n\n**No new \u03ba or positive eight-call primitive.** This is a fixed-word obstruction and reusable search filter in the inherited formal projective Clifford model. It does not close the general m=3, W=3, s=8 problem, infer formal linear independence from concrete 8-by-8 matrices, or extend to arbitrary circuit representations. The eight other whole words remain unclassified here.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Standard-library replay reconstructs all nine unresolved cases from the unchanged 73-word source corpus and verifies 919 exact certificates. Independent dense Gaussian multiplication/conjugation and symbolic paths agree on all 2,187 full paths, group classes, ranks and frames.\n- Three exact nine-call positive controls, 104 Laurent determinant controls, and mutations of cancellation homogeneity, valuation bounds, strict gaps and frame coverage pass.\n- Isolated relocated replay takes about 0.7 seconds locally. Equivalent gzip recompression is accepted; altered source/payload pins, incomplete coverage, a repinned zero-gap certificate and optimized Python are rejected. `validate.py` reproduces these controls.\n- Optional one-thread SciPy discovery regenerates all nine exclusion counts; its numerical outcomes are never trusted without exact rational verification. It is not needed for replay.\n- `make selected-record-check` passes. No full `make verify` or selected supplier cold replay is claimed for this standalone addition.\n\nReproduce:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B -S research/weighted-path-valuations/verify.py\npython3 -B -S research/weighted-path-valuations/validate.py\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_WEIGHTED_PATH_VALUATIONS` and `PASS_WEIGHTED_PATH_CLI_CONTROLS`.\n\nAll changes are confined to `research/weighted-path-valuations/`. Base: `66849e1475c930fd7732b1a0067ffee7e1e95f60`. Credits: littleBro's PR705 (`eeb0cd605415a73b792915aaa9185000f293c84a`) supplies the predecessor argument, unchanged corpus and `screen.py`; PR680 (`c3a5b6b7afec35d259c29bc2d8bb8516e975ad31`) supplies unchanged `model.py` and `dense.py`; eumemic's PR288 and the retained Swapnil Jain/upstream lineage supply the framework. All three source files and the corpus are byte-identical to the pinned PR705 head. `NOTICE.md` and `ORIGINS.json` retain attribution and exact pins.\n\nPrepared by Jeremy Diviney with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0; no literature-priority claim, independent human peer review or proof-assistant verification is asserted. Pre-submission overlap checks included PR720's distinct abelian bit theorem and PR791's distinct idempotent endpoint audit, with current metadata refreshed through PR799.\n",
